            free(img->pixels);  // NULL allocator = default behavior
        img->pixels = NULL;
    }
}
```

Wait — this is EXACTLY what the current code does! The problem is the `else free()` when `allocator` is non-NULL but `allocator->free` is NULL.

So the fix is simpler: just remove the `else free()` branch entirely. If `allocator` is non-NULL but `allocator->free` is NULL, calling `allocator->free(img->pixels)` will segfault, which is loud and correct.

```c
void KV_API ppm_image_free_with(struct Image* img, const struct PpmAllocator* allocator) {
    if (img) {
        if (allocator)
            allocator->free(img->pixels);
        else
            free(img->pixels);
        img->pixels = NULL;
    }
}
```

This way:
- `allocator == NULL` → `free()` (default, for `ppm_image_free`)
- `allocator != NULL, allocator->free != NULL` → uses custom free
- `allocator != NULL, allocator->free == NULL` → segfault (loud contract violation)

This matches the user's requirement. Let me present this as a plan.

Since plan mode is active, I can only present the plan, not make the edit. Let me do that.

